{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You pierced</b> the wicked one, king of the nations — the opposite of the salvation of Your anointed." "<b>With his rods, upon the wicked one alone you pierced his head</b> — that is, his head and king over his villages — <b>and behold now they storm</b>: they will shake, like <i>וְאֵסָרֵם</i> (and I will scatter them)." "And the meaning of <b>to scatter me</b>: to scatter Israel." "<b>Their exultation</b> — like <i>עָלַץ לְבָבִי</i> (my heart exults). And when he is scattered, the nations will devour them. And R. Moses said: they will rejoice, because the land of Israel will be hungry, for the poor man will eat his bread in secret, so that it not be snatched from him."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:57.334159323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}